# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
bin/*
Dockerfile.cross

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Go workspace file
go.work

# Kubernetes Generated files - skip generated files, except for vendored files
!vendor/**/zz_generated.*

# editor and IDE paraphernalia
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Kubeconfig might contain secrets
*.kubeconfig

# Coordinates for a live Databricks account. The live tests read these from the
# environment rather than a file precisely so that none of it can be committed:
# a host and an account id name somebody's account and the data in it.
.env
.env.*
.envrc
.databrickscfg

# Working notes. Not version controlled: they are a thinking record rather than
# a document, they go stale against the code within days, and nothing may link
# to them because a clone does not have them.
draft.md
draft/
notes/

# Working review notes. Same reason as draft.md.
review.md

# The state machine walk. Same reason as the others.
paths.md

# The list waiting to become GitHub issues. Same reason as the others: it is a
# thinking record, it goes stale against the code, and a clone does not have it.
issues.md

# This machine's own session state, and under it whole checkouts of this
# repository: .claude/worktrees/ holds one per agent. Untracked rather than
# ignored, a single `git add -A` commits every worktree into the tree it was
# made from.
.claude/

# The release artefact. `make build-installer` renders one consolidated manifest
# naming a published image; it is attached to a GitHub release rather than
# committed, so that what somebody applies is the one built from a tag.
dist/
